From: leonieziechmann <48921293+leonieziechmann@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:28:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] fix(data): the strict stop of a hydrated invoice lists
 the layout's findings; the flag auto

The verifier's findings on the fail-safe default (Q1):

- A hydrated invoice stopped on a finding of the layout (footer fit, the
  identity of number and date, a required part that renders nothing, the
  contrast of a themed(..) scope) with the bare message and no debug hint,
  and a data problem stopped before the layout was checked, so its stop
  did not list them. Now the strict stop of a hydrated invoice comes at the
  end of the invoice, once the layout has run (the second pass that every
  invoice makes), and lists every problem once, as many as the draft's
  report counts: the ones known up front (data, theme, measured) and the
  layout's, followed by the hint. Under hydrated strict those findings are
  emitted as in the draft, but no badge, marker or report is drawn; root
  attaches no e-invoice while an issue is open. The hint names the withheld
  e-invoice only when data is missing (a draft with theme or lint problems
  alone attaches its XML, as in 0.6.0). The identity check is a function,
  so that the stop reads its findings in the same pass. An invoice without
  data keeps the strict behaviour and texts of 0.6.0.
- `--input invoice-pro-validation=auto` is no override (the parameter
  decides) instead of "is not a validation level ... Did you mean auto?";
  the error for other values names auto.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
